---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Which Deal's Better?" description="How Which Deal's Better handles calculator entries, contact messages, analytics, advertising, and third-party services.">
  <section class="content-section"><div class="shell prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy describes how Which Deal's Better? handles information when you use the website.</p>
    <h2>Calculator entries</h2>
    <p>Prices, quantities, numbers of items in multipacks, product names, and units entered in the calculator are processed locally in your browser. They are not submitted to our servers and no account is required.</p>
    <h2>Contact messages</h2>
    <p>If you use the contact form, we process your name, email address, message, submission time, and limited technical information needed for security and delivery. We use this information to respond, prevent abuse, and operate the contact service. Messages are delivered through Brevo, which acts as an email service provider.</p>
    <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
    <p>The site may enable Google Analytics in the future to understand aggregate usage and may enable Google AdSense to support the site. If enabled, those services may use cookies or similar technologies and process device, browser, and usage information under their own policies. They are not currently configured unless their scripts appear on the site and any required consent choices are presented.</p>
    <h2>Cookies and third parties</h2>
    <p>The calculator does not need cookies. Third-party services may set cookies when analytics or advertising is enabled. Cloudflare processes requests as the website hosting and security provider. Brevo processes contact-email delivery.</p>
    <h2>Data choices</h2>
    <p>You can use the calculator without sending us personal information. To ask about a submitted contact message, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We avoid collecting information that is not needed to provide and protect the service.</p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy as the website or its services change. The date above shows the latest revision.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
